WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.840
Hey it’s Professor Dave; let’s work with
percentages.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.860
We are all aware of percentages, as they are
ubiquitous in society.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.470
There is a sale today, thirty percent off.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:20.350
Leave a twenty percent tip after the meal.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.650
Today there is a fifty percent chance of rain.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.300
So what are these things?

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:31.190
Well in Latin, centum means one hundred, so
percent literally means out of a hundred.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:37.440
It’s just a way of conveying magnitude,
by modifying some total into a hundred, and

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.550
then reporting a value of interest as some
fraction of that hundred.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:49.530
If you get a ninety percent on your math quiz,
you could have gotten nine points out of ten,

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:54.719
eighteen points out of twenty, four hundred
fifty out of five hundred, or any other number

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:58.629
that obeys this ratio of ninety out of a hundred.

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:03.600
Whatever we have to do to the larger number
to make it one hundred, we do that same thing

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.600
to the other number.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:12.580
Ten must be multiplied by ten to get a hundred,
so the nine is also multiplied by ten.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:19.100
In this way, percentages are ratios, they
are just very specific ratios that compare

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:24.909
numbers to a hundred, because although this
number is totally arbitrary, it is an ideal

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:27.359
size for comparison.

00:01:27.359 --> 00:01:33.760
One hundred is small enough that our brains
can easily comprehend its magnitude, but also

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:40.640
large enough that there are sufficient gradations
between zero and a hundred so as to make meaningful

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.340
comparisons.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:47.549
In this way, we can look at percentages as
simple fractions.

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:50.850
Eighty percent is eighty one-hundredths.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:55.939
We learned how to simplify fractions, so let’s
divide both of these numbers by twenty.

00:01:55.939 --> 00:01:58.530
We should get four fifths.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:05.009
This means that eighty percent and four fifths
are equivalent; they mean the same thing.

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:10.789
Moving to another example, fifty percent is
fifty one hundredths, and dividing both numbers

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:13.980
by fifty, we get one half.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.599
This makes sense, as fifty is half of a hundred.

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:22.739
If you have something like three percent,
that will be three one hundredths, and that

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:25.930
can’t be simplified any further.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:32.319
We should be able to convert between percentages,
fractions, and even decimals in this way with

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:35.020
relative ease, so let’s check comprehension.

